WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.735
Hi, I'm Morgan, and today

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:04.838
I'm going to be showing you
how I’m using Photoshop’s new Generative Fill

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:08.208
partner models to streamline
my workflow as a graphic designer.

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:11.911
Specifically, I'm going to be showing you
how I'm using Nano Banana, Gemini

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:16.883
2.5 Flash Image, and Flux Context Pro
to make mockups for my clients.

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:20.320
So to start, I thought I'd show you
this photo that my client sent me today.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.756
Yeah, haha. 

00:00:22.756 --> 00:00:25.992
They asked me if I could mock up
the designs that we've been working on

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:28.995
onto their actual bottle
because they received a sample.

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:32.132
Now, the forward that they've sent me
is very low fi.

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:33.833
It's not very high quality

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:36.836
and we're not going to have
a very polished final result.

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:40.440
I thought about maybe
just adding the design to this,

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.242
which would be super easy to do.

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:47.247
I could just drag it in as I normally
would and do some warping.

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:50.250
So let's just see how that looks for
talking sake.

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.151
I mean, it's fine.

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:53.787
It's not great though.

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:57.123
I feel like we could have
a much more polished finish

00:00:57.857 --> 00:01:00.827
if we utilize some of Adobe
Photoshop’s new features.

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:03.830
So I'm going to go ahead and select
the Rectangular Marquee Tool,

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:07.867
and I'm going to head into the Generative
Fill option in the contextual task bar.

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:12.105
and I'm going to select Gemini 2.5
Nano Banana.

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:14.774
So in here
I am just going to give it a prompt

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:19.412
and nano banana is really good
at understanding prompts

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:21.014
and being contextually aware.

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:23.516
So you're going to get
a lot of your details preserved

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:24.918
if you ask it to do that.

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:29.522
So I'm going to go ahead and say remove
the hands, remove the background, place

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.224
the bottle into a clean white studio

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:34.227
background with studio lighting
product photography style,

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.462
and we'll just see what it does.

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:39.399
Hopefully what it's going to do
is tidy up this image

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:42.402
and get rid of all the mess
in the background.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.905
Okay, so already

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:50.043
you can see that the output is so much
better than the image that I was sent.

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:51.811
Wow.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:54.781
So you can see that it's done
a pretty good job, and it's preserved

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:56.516
all the details in the shape
from the bottle,

00:01:56.516 --> 00:02:00.120
but I actually need three bottles
because my client has three flavors

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.722
of this product.
So I'm going to go up to Object Select

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:05.725
and I'm just going to make
a really quick selection of this bottle

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:09.462
and I'm just going to duplicate that
very roughly.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:12.165
I'm not being too precious about it,

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:15.969
and I'm just going to drag that
so that they are side by side.

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:20.106
So then I'm going to go ahead
and grab the Rectangular Marquee again.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.776
And I'm basically just going to ask

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:27.046
Generative Fill to unify this image.

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:31.384
So I'm going to go ahead and select
Flux Context Pro.

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:35.388
And Flux Context Pro is really good
because it's contextually aware.

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:37.123
It's got advanced contextual awareness

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:38.024
so it's going to preserve

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:41.060
all the details that I ask it to
and hopefully give us a good output.

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:44.964
So I'm just going to ask it
to unify the image so that all the bottles

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:47.967
are on a white studio background together.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:50.503
Don't change the bottles and add subtle
shadows.

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:51.004
Okay. Wow.

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:53.306
So this has already saved me
a ton of time.

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:55.341
This was taking me so long to do before.

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:58.344
And now I can focus
on the actual detail work.

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:00.947
So I'm quite happy with this output.

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:04.884
I'm going to go ahead and drag
all of my label artwork into the file,

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:08.821
and I've got this in SVG form,
so once I've dropped them in I'm

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:12.725
just going to select all three
and shrink them down to size together.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.762
So I'm going to basically put

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:19.832
my first flavor here, that flavor there,

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:21.434
and this flavor in the middle.

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:26.172
And super quickly what I'm going to do
is convert all of these to small objects

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:30.176
and this will just allow me
to not only switch out that artwork

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:32.345
if it gets changed,
or if my client has any revisions,

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:35.348
but also to warp this
to fit the bottle slightly.

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:38.785
So I'm going to click warp,
and then I'm just going to go up to warp

00:03:38.785 --> 00:03:41.788
and select arc lower

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:44.224
and you can see that
it's kept the top straight

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:47.594
because the bottle at the top is straight,
but the bottom has a slight curve to it.

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:50.096
And this just makes it feel
a little bit more realistic.

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:51.564
So I'm going to go ahead and do that
to the rest of the bottles.

00:03:51.564 --> 00:03:53.066
Okay cool. 

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:56.202
So now that I've done that
and everything is looking a little bit

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:57.837
more realistic, I'm going to go ahead and 

00:03:57.837 --> 00:04:01.474
select all of the labels
and change the blend mode to multiply.

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:03.509
And this is just going to allow
the shadows and light

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:04.544
in from the image below

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:07.747
to come through the artwork and make it
look just a little bit less flat.

00:04:07.814 --> 00:04:08.581
Okay, cool.

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:10.383
So this is looking really good.

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:13.253
The only thing I need to change
now is the lid color, because the lids

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:16.756
are going to have a color that corresponds
to the flavor of the bottle.

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:21.060
So I'm going to go ahead and use
the Rectangular Marquee once again,

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:24.697
and I'm just going to go in here
and create a new layer.

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:27.934
So I'm going to select the pink from here,

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:33.306
and then I'm just going to use the Fill
Bucket Tool, fill in that marquee, deselect

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:35.508
and then I'm going to set the blend mode
to multiply again.

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:37.710
This is obviously really rough

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.647
and you can go in
and maybe add a slight feather to this.

00:04:40.647 --> 00:04:42.849
But because this is a mock
up for my client,

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:44.517
this is just a really quick visual

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:48.588
that doesn't need to be perfect, but
we want it to be as polished as possible.

00:04:48.688 --> 00:04:51.257
So now I'm going to go ahead and do that
to the rest of the bottles.

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:55.161
So mocking this up to be so realistic
would have taken me so long before,

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:58.231
but I was able to do it in a matter
of minutes using Generative Fills

00:04:58.231 --> 00:05:02.402
new partner models in Adobe Photoshop,
Nano Banana and Flux Context Pro,

00:05:02.535 --> 00:05:06.239
and also my own Photoshop skills
to make it just a little bit more refined.

00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:10.943
And you can see that we've gone from this
to this, and it's come quite a long way

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:14.347
I must say, and that's something that I'd
definitely be proud to show my client.

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:16.849
You can try these features
out in Adobe Photoshop today.

